    <section class="section"><div class="wrap content"><p class="eyebrow">A Victorian home in Victoria West</p><h2>A house with a story to tell.</h2><p>Moonlight Manor is described in guesthouse listings as a Victorian home dating to the late 1800s. Its original Oregon floors, high ceilings, sash windows, shuttered doors and veranda preserve the character of another era.</p><p>Today, the house welcomes travellers looking for a comfortable and peaceful stay in the Upper Karoo. Rooms are furnished with antiques and open towards the veranda or garden.</p><p>Our aim for this website is to celebrate the property’s heritage while making it easy for guests to discover the rooms, explore the area and enquire about a stay.</p><p class="muted">Historical details and ownership story to be confirmed with the owners before final publication.</p><a class="btn" href="/accommodation/">Explore the rooms</a></div></section>
